<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#old-uyghur-language">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Uyghur language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> was the Turkic language of the Uyghur Kingdom of Qocho and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> Uyghurs from the 9th to the 14th centuries. Written mainly in the Old Uyghur script, derived from Sogdian, it was the language of a large Buddhist, Manichaean and Christian literature, much of it translated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a>, Tocharian, Chinese and Sogdian. Its script later became the basis of the Mongolian alphabet.</p></div>
